/ A dependency panel: a name, a headline figure, a state colour and a few
/ supporting numbers. Deliberately small and calm — these are the panels that
/ stay green during the incident, and their job is to be quietly reassuring
/ while the finding above them is not.
.cell-auto.card.p-4.column.gap-3 class="ring-1 ring-white/5"
  .row.items-center.justify-between
    span.text-xs.uppercase.tracking-wider.text-gray-500
      = title
    span class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider #{ observatory_state_class(state) }"
      = state == :unknown ? 'no data' : state
  .row.items-baseline.gap-2
    span class="text-2xl font-light #{ observatory_state_class(state) }"
      = headline
    - if defined?(subtitle) && subtitle.present?
      span.text-xs.text-gray-500
        = subtitle
  - if defined?(ratio) && !ratio.nil?
    = observatory_bar(ratio, state: state)
  - if defined?(rows) && rows.present?
    .column class="gap-1 text-xs"
      - rows.each do |label, value|
        .row.justify-between.gap-4
          span.text-gray-500 = label
          span.text-gray-300 = value
